From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:08:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/21] media: apple: vxd: fix the open() NULL dereference and harden
 the V4L2 paths

Round 2 (warm kexec, apple_vxd.boot_firmware unset) registered
/dev/video0, then udev's v4l_id oopsed in its first open(): NULL
dereference at VA 0, read (ESR 0x96000004, level-0 translation fault).

Root cause: struct apple_vxd_variant carried coded_fmts/num_coded_fmts
since the V4L2 patch, but s8000_vxd_variant never filled them, and no
other code did either.  open() -> apple_vxd_reset_coded_fmt() took
&variant->coded_fmts[0] == NULL and read ->fourcc (offset 0) from it.
Round 1 never registered the node, so the bug only showed once round 2
wired V4L2 into probe.  The other candidate, a NULL vdev->dev_parent in
v4l_querycap(), is not a bug: video_register_device() defaults it to
v4l2_dev->dev, and media_set_bus_info() handles NULL anyway.

The coded-format table now lives in the device, filled by
apple_vxd_h264_register() during probe.  apple_vxd_v4l2_init() and
open() refuse to run without it (-ENODEV).  Every path reachable from
open, release, QUERYCAP, ENUM_FMT, G_FMT, TRY_FMT and S_FMT on the video
and media nodes was audited with the firmware not booted.  None of them
touches state that only the firmware boot or the debugfs trigger
creates.  The only hw_ready consumer is the H.264 job path, which fails
the job with -EAGAIN.

Also fixed along those paths:
- G_FMT on the output queue returned num_planes 0 and sizeimage 0 by
  default.  It now gets the same normalization as TRY_FMT: one plane,
  1 MiB.
- v4l2_ready was set right after video_register_device(), so a later
  registration failure left remove() a second teardown.  It is set
  last now, and the error labels no longer clean up a media device that
  was never initialized.
- A V4L2 registration failure used to fail the probe after debugfs
  existed, freeing vxd (devm) under live debugfs files.  The probe now
  logs the failure and continues without the node.
- bus_info is no longer hardcoded.  The core fills
  "platform:<dev_name>" for both QUERYCAP and the media device, so the
  two match.
- The debugfs mbox/regs dumps read MMIO without a runtime PM reference.
  The block autosuspends 100 ms after probe, so a pre-boot `cat` read an
  unpowered block.  Both dumps now resume the device around the read.
- apple_vxd_boot_firmware() released the firmware a second time on
  every failure after the copy, for example a ready-poll timeout, which
  is the likely T3 outcome.
- W=1: drop the unused 'saved' in vxd_discover_core() (the register read
  is kept) and the static/extern mismatch on apple_vxd_log_pwrstate().
- TRY_EXT_CTRLS on the current control values failed with -EINVAL.  The
  SPS validator allow-listed profile_idc 66/77/100, so the default SPS
  (profile_idc 0) was rejected.  It now rejects only the profiles the
  decoder lacks: extended, SVC, and MVC/stereo/depth.  High 10, 4:2:2
  and 4:4:4 stay rejected by the chroma and bit-depth checks.  Found by
  v4l2-compliance.

New bring-up aids:
- apple_vxd.v4l2=0 skips the V4L2 registration entirely.  Probe, GART,
  debugfs and the boot trigger still work.
- Every V4L2 entry point announces itself with a flushed dev_emerg STEP
  line.  That covers open/release (with the caller's comm/pid), every
  ioctl before the core runs (named, e.g. "ioctl VIDIOC_QUERYCAP"), the
  driver handler, mmap, start/stop_streaming, device_run, and the media
  request validate/queue hooks.  The high-rate lines can be silenced at
  runtime with /sys/module/apple_vxd/parameters/step_ioctls.
- A register-time self-test runs before any node is exposed.  It
  covers the driver half of open() (format defaults, the m2m context
  and vb2 queues, and the control handler including
  v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup -> s_ctrl), every format, enum and
  framesize handler body, the querycap fill and the driver half of
  release(), all on a private context.  A failure names the check and
  skips the V4L2 registration instead of oopsing under udev.  The
  handler bodies now take the context, and the file-based ioctl ops
  are thin wrappers around them.  The v4l2_fh bookkeeping is core code
  and is not run.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
